## Improvements

- [PROMPT] The `<verification>` block's three spec-name greps (`go test ./pkg -v 2>&1 | grep -c '...'`) return **0** even for correct implementations, because Ginkgo v2's default reporter prints dots (`•`), not spec descriptions, under plain `go test -v`. Spec names only appear with `-ginkgo.v` added (`go test ./pkg -v -ginkgo.v`). The four new specs were verified present and green that way (105/105 specs pass); the literal verification command as written cannot distinguish present-but-dot-rendered specs from missing ones.
- [GUIDE] `go-testing-guide.md` should note that for Ginkgo v2 suites, dark-factory verification greps on `It` descriptions must use `go test ./pkg -v -ginkgo.v` (or `-ginkgo.v`), not bare `go test ./pkg -v` — otherwise acceptance greps fail spuriously and waste an audit cycle.
